$DIR/test.p:7:30: cannot convert non-constant n (variable of type int) to enum type Color without a check: use the comma-ok form (v, ok := Color(...))
    A number that is not a constant may not be the value of any member, so
    converting it to an enum needs a check. Use the comma-ok form: ok reports
    whether the number is a member's value.
    Go allows any integer in a named integer type. Plutonium enums are closed
    sets, so a value outside the set is caught where it enters, not later in a
    switch.
    Use the comma-ok form:
        c, ok := Color(n)
        if !ok {
            return errBadColor
        }
    (see "Enums" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.12)
    (run "pluto explain E2314" for a longer explanation)
